# CITATION.cff — GitHub Citation File Format
# https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# Place at the repo root as CITATION.cff. GitHub renders a "Cite this
# repository" button, and Zenodo reads these fields when minting a DOI.
 
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "motor-thermal-deeplearning: Deep learning for rotor temperature estimation in electric traction motors"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of LSTM, GRU, and MLP virtual sensors for rotor
  temperature estimation in permanent-magnet synchronous motors, trained and
  evaluated on the public Paderborn University PMSM dataset with
  leave-one-profile-out cross-validation. A clean-room, open-data companion
  to the author's published work on data-driven thermal modeling for
  electrically excited and rare-earth-free synchronous motors.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23407318"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FarzanehTatari/motor-thermal-deeplearning"
keywords:
  - thermal estimation
  - virtual sensor
  - PMSM
  - electric motor
  - LSTM
  - GRU
  - deep learning
  - automotive
authors:
  - family-names: Tatari
    given-names: Farzaneh
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5176-3372"
